      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how seductive that peace can be when exhaustion makes the cliff feel like a soft landing instead of a drop. But what you're describing isn't the wind calling you—it's your own tired mind whispering in fog's voice, and that whisper isn't the same as truth. You don't have to finish the story today, or fight the wind; you only have to take one small step back from the edge and let someone help you carry the weight for a while. The journey may feel over, but you deserve to see what the next chapter might hold if you stay.",
